    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "would require documentary proof of citizenship to register to vote in the United States in a federal election. It's necessary because currently the law prohibits states from checking that. We had multiple hearings. It's clearly necessary. There are clearly non-citizens voting. They clearly need to help in the states to solve the problem. So it's an important bill. And it's an important bill for this election, because it would take effect immediately. It would stick penalties immediately. And there's registration up through same day, election day in 22 states. So we thought it was important. President Trump thought it was important. So I worked with the speaker. We created a situation where we had the freedom caucus to get a visual position. President Trump wanted it. The speaker wanted it. So we decided to put together something we thought we could move forward that while not perfect, would actually accomplish the objective. Now, what was that? a continuing resolution, not my favorite vehicle, but we cannot get all the appropriations bills done by September 30. So it would freeze spending at current levels, levels that I don't love, through March. Now why is that important? Because it takes the pen away from Chuck Schumer, and it takes the pen away from Joe Biden slash whoever the hell is running the White",
