  {
    "episode_id": 91315,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91315.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "And it would give the pen to Donald Trump and Republicans in March. So we were going to take that, add the save back to it, and then force a fight in September. President Trump supported that play, I supported that play. So it all got through, and then yesterday I'm going to pass forward to the end. Unfortunately, for reasons that I think were based in principle, although I think misguided, some of my more conservative friends, about 14, 16 of them, voted against it because they don't like CR. They don't want to fund the current level of government. Now look, I started the don't defund tyranny exercise two years ago. I literally branded that. Went after the IRS, went after DHS. I still feel that way. But when it gets to the five weeks before election day, I don't think we're going to have the ability to have Mike Johnson in the moderate shut the government down. That would be my preference. I'm happy to run on that. But there's some of my colleagues who won't. So I was like, let's pick a fight on the Save Act. And then when the Democrats jam us on that, we'll just have to make a decision. Do we shut it down and fight on it? Or do we then move to saying, look, we'll take a six-month CR, you won't get the say back, and then we'll live to fight in November, but we won't have to deal with all those crime in December. So now the result of that bill failing. We had almost 200 Republicans who voted for it, about 16 who voted against. The result now is I'm afraid we're going to get a continuing resolution into December with nothing else and then leave town. That's the high likelihood of what I'm being told next week, which means we won't be able to have a, you know, take it up to September 30th fight over the Save Act. And now we're just going to have to go campaign on it. That's what I think is going to happen. It's not fully decided.",
