  {
    "episode_id": 91315,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91315.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "District 21 and Republican, the great state of Texas, it's Chip Roy. Let's spend a little time on what you said about, we know that people who are not allowed to vote are voting. Non-citizens, because people here, you say that in scream, if they're on the left, they'll scream, he's lying, what a liar, nobody's voting, nobody who's not a citizen's vote, that's just, It's demonstrably true that they are. I mean, even here in Texas, Ken Paxton just went through the rolls and we've got people who are voting illegally. We also know that in other states that they've found them, and I think Oregon just announced a few days ago, which is an odd place, where they do only mail-in voting. It turns out, oh, we accidentally had people who are here illegally or who weren't citizens that were voting. Don't worry, we took care of it. If they admit to 300, it's probably more like 30,000. So we know that it's happening. If you don't mind, spend a minute or so on that that you have actual fact and proof that people who are not allowed to vote in the federal elections are.",
